          <name>SYSMEM_ACC_TYPE</name>
          <description>SYSMEM access error type</description>
          <addressOffset>0x10FC</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>TYPE</name>
              <description>SRAM access error type. This field will be cleared along with the corresponding flag clear.  [4] - CBUS Access Error [3] - SBUS Access Error [2] - Write Error [1] - Read Error [0] - Fetch Error  Note: Under the rare condition of both CBUS and SBUS access errors occurring at the same time, bit[4] and bit[3] will be set together to indicate the same, but bits[2:0] (as well as SYSMEM_ACC_ADDR) will convey information only realted to the CBUS access error. Under this condition, the CBUS access error has to be debugged, fixed and rerun before proceeding to debug the SBUS access error.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>5</bitWidth>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
